Sectoare de activitate: Bănci, Bănci de investiții și Telecomunicații
About our team 
 BCR is the place where you learn, grow, and contribute to shaping the future of banking. We are recognized as a school of excellence in banking, a top employer in the banking sector, and a team open to learning, where every colleague feels seen and valued.
 We are an organization that values people and supports them in having a life that brings fulfillment, security, and balance.
 We are looking for a highly experienced Senior Network Engineer who can design, challenge, secure and evolve complex enterprise network environments. This is a strategic and hands-on role. You will act as a trusted technical authority, shaping the architecture of large-scale datacenter and hybrid-cloud infrastructures, while ensuring that network design decisions support security-by-design principles, operational excellence and cyber resilience.
 This role requires deep technical expertise, strong analytical capabilities and the confidence to challenge existing designs, identify risks and influence critical infrastructure decisions across multiple technology domains.
 How you will contribute 
Act as a trusted advisor for Network, Security and Infrastructure Architecture initiatives, driving technical decisions and engineering best practices;
Design and optimize Enterprise, Datacenter and Hybrid-Cloud network architectures, ensuring scalability, performance, resilience and security; 
Serve as a senior technical authority for architecture standards, connectivity models and network design across distributed environments;
Analyze end-to-end communication flows and translate business and security requirements into scalable network solutions;
Design and implement advanced networking technologies, including Routing & Switching, TCP/IP, BGP, OSPF, VLAN/VRF, DNS, Load Balancers, Proxies and Reverse Proxies;
Develop secure Internet-facing, Datacenter and DMZ architectures, minimizing exposure and operational risk;
Apply Zero Trust and Defense-in-Depth principles through effective segmentation and secure connectivity between network zones;
Review and optimize connectivity requirements, identifying attack paths, architectural weaknesses and opportunities for infrastructure hardening;
Collaborate with Cybersecurity, Cloud, Infrastructure and Application teams to ensure secure and resilient enterprise connectivity;
Engineer highly available environments through redundancy, failover and resilience mechanisms, supporting Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery objectives; 
Participate in the resolution of complex infrastructure and cybersecurity incidents, performing root-cause analysis and driving continuous improvement;
Promote an automation-first approach based on Git → Automation → Validation → Deployment → Continuous Verification.
 What will help you be successful 
Deep expertise in Cisco Enterprise & Datacenter Networking, Routing & Switching, TCP/IP, BGP and OSPF;
Strong hands-on experience with Firewalls, Security Gateways, Load Balancers, DNS/IPAM and DMZ architectures;
Advanced understanding of Network Segmentation (VLAN/VRF), Datacenter Connectivity and Hybrid-Cloud Networking;
Proven experience with Network Automation using Ansible, Python, REST APIs, Terraform and Git;
Strong knowledge of Network Observability, Telemetry and Performance Monitoring; 
Ability to troubleshoot and resolve complex networking challenges across distributed enterprise environments;
Engineering mindset focused on automation, scalability, resilience and security by design;
Most importantly, proven experience as an L3/L4 Network Engineer, capable of solving complex technical problems and making sound architectural decisions in large-scale enterprise environments.
 Sounds like you'd be a good fit? Well, check out what we provide for our people 
Monthly budget for flexible benefits through the Benefit Online platform;
13th month salary;
Performance-based bonus;
Banking facilities, benefits for private pension and discounts on insurance policies;
Gifts for special occasions; 
Vacation allowance;
Private medical services for you and your family;
Hybrid and flexible work schedule;
1 month / per year of remote work from abroad (UE);
Up to 27 vacation days depending on your professional experience;
Extra 7 days off per year if you have used up your vacation days;
One day off for your birthday;
Wellbeing, personal and professional development programs, and platforms that allow you to learn anytime, anywhere, and from any device;
Subscription to Bookster.
 To find out how BCR processes the personal data required in the recruitment process, please visit https://www.bcr.ro/ro/cariere/informare-candidati.
